WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:05.760
Today we are going to see how AI research&nbsp;
is changing the landscape of gaming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.640
videoconferencing, robotics, and so much more.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.240
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.840
Now, first - here, we usually talk about papers.&nbsp;
This is not a paper. So you will see results&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:27.080
that we cannot evaluate as thoroughly as we&nbsp;
normally do with peer-reviewed research. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:33.240
I still think it is important to talk about&nbsp;
because even though this is not paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.760
but it is Papers coming to life&nbsp;
in the world around us. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:44.640
these technologies appeared or will appear&nbsp;
in products that millions of Fellow Scholars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.600
are going to use all around the world,&nbsp;
so I would like to show them to you.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.080
And I will note that we have&nbsp;
no business ties with NVIDIA.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:01:00.440
Now, here they talked about HybridAI, where&nbsp;
your local graphics card will do one part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:07.600
of the computation, and a different part&nbsp;
will be streamed from the cloud. So, why?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.360
Well, for instance, noise removal for your&nbsp;
videoconferencing should run locally on your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:22.440
machine as it requires low latency, it cannot&nbsp;
wait for the cloud to do all this. There is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:28.880
enough time for that. But Photoshop’s generative&nbsp;
fill can take a little longer in the cloud to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.960
ensure it runs on a smarter AI model, and&nbsp;
give you your text to image results here.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:43.280
Okay, so these are the local and cloud models.&nbsp;
What is this hybrid thing? Well, consider their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:50.520
previous work on creating virtual characters with&nbsp;
generative AI. Earlier, they showcased a system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:57.840
which can automatically come up with dialogue&nbsp;
for a virtual character in a video game. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:05.840
the text what the character needs to say will be&nbsp;
synthesized by an AI, then a text to voice AI will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:13.120
make it actually say it in a human voice, and the&nbsp;
mouth movements will also be synthesized. Look.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:28.520
It sounded a little stiff, could have been a&nbsp;
bit more natural, but this is only the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:34.520
version of something that was previously nearly&nbsp;
impossible. So here’s the breakdown. When you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:41.160
talk to a virtual character, your local voice&nbsp;
input is transcribed locally, this then goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:48.280
into a large language model in the cloud, when&nbsp;
we got the text response from the game character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:54.040
speech is synthesized in the cloud, and then,&nbsp;
it comes back to your machine where the lip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.040 --> 00:03:00.920
syncing is done quickly and locally. And all&nbsp;
this happens without you noticing all this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:07.720
wizardry. That is quite impressive. And this&nbsp;
is available for developers to use right now.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:14.280
We can also use generative AI to create these&nbsp;
virtual characters themselves too. Like the video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:21.280
game characters from this earlier video, they can&nbsp;
all be given an identity and a backstory and like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:28.480
good little actors, they will pretend to be this&nbsp;
person. They can even become a Fellow Scholar.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.760
Now at this point my reaction was&nbsp;
that I’d love to see that in action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:37.760
in this framework and luckily,&nbsp;
that’s exactly what happened.&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:52.960
Now these characters are much more true to life,&nbsp;
and it gets better, every time you enter the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.800
the conversation will be different. All&nbsp;
synthesized on the fly. If the occasion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:05.400
calls for it, words are connected to actions&nbsp;
as well, and you might get a drink for free.

